{"version":"1","id":"javaworld","handle":"javaworld","name":"Java World","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/7c31b925037d4e5693aad86b1eba70aa","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-5.8045,"y":-2.0508,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":198,"newest_post_at":"2024-06-26T18:00:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2020-07-23T08:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.002525,"listicle_ratio":0.015152,"question_ratio":0.025253,"avg_read_time":6.121212,"summary_length_avg":301.21978,"title_length_avg":46.39899,"title_length_var":116.845858,"tag_entropy":3.566552,"tag_diversity":0.59596,"top_tag_share":0.424242,"avg_upvotes":1.277778,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.075758,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.062992,"zero_engagement_share":0.515152,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.968266,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.081967},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-2.5147,5.5588],"cadence_depth":[2.9265,0.5588],"hype_variety":[-2.9853,3.9265],"title_style":[2.2941,4.3529]},"top_tags":[["java",167],["general-programming",39],["oracle",23],["jdk",18],["javascript",17],["python",15],["devtools",14],["kotlin",14]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["7 reasons Java is still great","JDK 23: The new features in Java 23","Oracle JDK Mission Control 9 adds dark theme, configurable JVM browser"],"outlier":["Visual Studio Code 1.78 debuts profile templates for Python, Java, Angular"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"FXgwewzMX","title":"OpenJDK proposal would bring value classes and objects to Java","url":"https://www.infoworld.com/article/3715642/openjdk-proposal-would-bring-value-classes-and-objects-to-java.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/openjdk-proposal-would-bring-value-classes-and-objects-to-java-fxgwewzmx","summary":"An OpenJDK proposal is set to introduce value classes and objects to Java, allowing for class instances with only final fields and no object identity. This would enable objects to be differentiated by their field values, improve memory footprint, locality, and garbage collection efficiency. The proposal, updated in June 2022, does not yet specify a target version for Java and will not introduce a struct feature or change the treatment of primitive types.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4caf546547b3bc71f1abb8e24a03b839?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":7,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-26T18:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"8e4rhDBkA","title":"Java\u2019s Project Leyden arrives in early-access build","url":"https://www.infoworld.com/article/3715562/javas-project-leyden-arrives-in-early-access-build.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/java-s-project-leyden-arrives-in-early-access-build-8e4rhdbka","summary":"Project Leyden from OpenJDK has released its first early-access build focused on improving Java application startup time. Highlights include ahead-of-time (AOT) compilation for better code execution, archived method profiles for quicker performance, a unified Cache Data Store for optimization artifacts, and generation of dynamic proxies and reflection data. Developers are encouraged to provide feedback via the Project Leyden mailing list.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ba0a89adebdceae93c85b28d9f039cec?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-25T15:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"wYJjJI0kS","title":"Polymorphism and inheritance in Java","url":"https://www.infoworld.com/article/3290403/java-challengers-3-polymorphism-and-inheritance.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/polymorphism-and-inheritance-in-java-wyjjji0ks","summary":"Learn about polymorphism and inheritance in Java and how to use it in your programs.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/a305bb391f06ae07451cb35f3cf1ee92?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-13T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"ylawMZjoJ","title":"What's wrong with Java's sun.misc.Unsafe?","url":"https://www.infoworld.com/article/3715492/whats-wrong-with-javas-sunmiscunsafe.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-s-wrong-with-java-s-sun-misc-unsafe--ylawmzjoj","summary":"Java's sun.misc.Unsafe class has been in use since 2002 and provides low-level methods for developers. However, it has problems related to JVM maintainability and is not safe to use. A newer JEP proposes to remove Unsafe's memory access methods, and this article explores the class, reasons for deprecation, alternatives, and the need for solutions. It also emphasizes the importance of refactoring and the challenges in replacing Unsafe's capabilities.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/74df756226d6374c12949a0c258a3a2d?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-12T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"aqBLaLGA1","title":"Does Java pass by reference or pass by value?","url":"https://www.infoworld.com/article/3512039/does-java-pass-by-reference-or-pass-by-value.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/does-java-pass-by-reference-or-pass-by-value--aqblalga1","summary":"This post discusses the concept of passing by reference and passing by value in Java, specifically for object parameters. It explains that Java passes object references by value, and provides examples of passing object references, passing primitive types, passing immutable object references, and passing mutable object references. The post also includes tips on what to avoid and what to remember when passing Java object references.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/62867327a52db7826020d27380aac31e?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2024-06-06T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"DOsJ6M68Y","title":"Inheritance in Java, Part 1: The extends keyword","url":"https://www.infoworld.com/article/2987426/java-101-inheritance-in-java-part-1.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/inheritance-in-java-part-1-the-extends-keyword-dosj6m68y","summary":"This post discusses inheritance in Java, including what it is, single inheritance vs. multiple inheritance, and how to use the extends keyword.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4771a0c0b214018ca0300e2c8ce250ad?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-04T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"x43kWiRwZ","title":"Inheritance in Java, Part 2: Object and its methods","url":"https://www.infoworld.com/article/2987584/java-101-inheritance-in-java-part-2.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/inheritance-in-java-part-2-object-and-its-methods-x43kwirwz","summary":"Learn about the Object class in Java and its methods, how to extend it, and what the getClass() method does.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d434c10536e9900fa529637fd1bc0c02?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-04T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"XX8tMvWXm","title":"IBM previews watsonx Code Assistant for Enterprise Java Applications","url":"https://www.infoworld.com/article/3715485/ibm-previews-watsonx-code-assistant-for-enterprise-java-applications.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ibm-previews-watsonx-code-assistant-for-enterprise-java-applications-xx8tmvwxm","summary":"IBM previews watsonx Code Assistant for Enterprise Java Applications, an AI-based code assistant that improves developer productivity by navigating complex code structures, describing changes needed, implementing code and configuration changes, and maintaining critical application functions with generative AI.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/dce60c78d4e5ae9714ecbfeeccadc517?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-21T13:21:00.000Z"},{"id":"dEAYZHPmD","title":"Comparing Java objects with equals() and hashcode()","url":"https://www.infoworld.com/article/3305792/comparing-java-objects-with-equals-and-hashcode.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/comparing-java-objects-with-equals-and-hashcode--deayzhpmd","summary":"Java's equals() and hashcode() methods are important for comparing and identifying objects in Java programs. This post explains why it is necessary to override these methods, how to use them to compare objects, and their role in collections. It also provides guidelines and rules for using equals() and hashcode().","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/b88049dda4cdbd336dbbbc02c9b13bf9?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-16T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"Yh9kJ3aqO","title":"Take advantage of user-defined variables in JavaScript","url":"https://www.infoworld.com/article/2077113/take-advantage-of-user-defined-variables-in-javascript.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/take-advantage-of-user-defined-variables-in-javascript-yh9kj3aqo","summary":"Learn how to use user-defined variables in JavaScript to store and manipulate different types of data, such as numbers, strings, Boolean values, and objects. Discover the rules for naming variables and understand the scope of variables in JavaScript.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6bec5660a3994b38b2628a92446f3126?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":7,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-15T09:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["securityscorecard","cloudonaut","apollo","smallstep","ermetic"],"opposite_handles":["tbpn","alexfinn","ryolu_","felixrieseberg","kloss_xyz"],"similar":[{"id":"securityscorecard","handle":"securityscorecard","name":"SecurityScorecard","is_squad":false,"x":-5.7763,"y":-1.8745,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":245,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/919309ba524740269b03cdf6fec44b85","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":2.714371,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.008163,"avg_read_time":4.134